# .dockerignore for the Firestarter demo: what the build may see.
#
# ALLOWLIST: start by excluding everything, then let in only what the
# Dockerfile COPYs. A new file or folder in the repo root (a venv, a bundle
# ZIP, a secret, generated data) stays out unless it's added here.
# Rules are read top to bottom; the last matching rule wins.

*

# --- Let in: what the Dockerfile COPYs ---
!pyproject.toml
!alembic.ini
!run.py
!docker-entrypoint.sh
!app
!migrations
!scripts/bootstrap_demo.py
# the demo starter kit: inputs only
!data/topology.xlsx
!data/services
!data/compliance
!data/simulation
# test stage only (docker build --target test); never in the runtime image
!tests

# --- Shut out again: what doesn't belong inside those folders ---

# Python caches
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache

# Generated output that can sit in a local data/ folder
data/compliance/reports

# Environment data never lives in the code tree (ADR 0001); a cheap net in
# case some turns up anyway: workbooks, pickles, device configs, logs,
# databases, bundle files. (tests/ keeps its fixture workbook, data/ its inputs.)
app/**/*.xlsx
app/**/*.pkl
app/**/*.cfg
app/**/*.log*
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
**/*.sqlite*
**/manifest.json
